        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Americas</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Fall of Tenochtitlan</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">May to 13 August 1521 (Julian date); the three Spanish forces took up their positions on 22 May and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> surrendered on 13 August</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, the island capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a>, and the causeways and lakeside towns round it, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Spaniards under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a>, with 84 horsemen, 194 crossbowmen and arquebusiers, 650 foot soldiers, thirteen sloops and 20,000 warriors from Tlaxcala, Huexotzinco and Cholula, besieged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> under their tlatoani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a>; Cortés's own letter puts his allies at the end at more than 150,000 against some 900 Spaniards</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> surrendered on 13 August 1521 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuauhtemoc">Cuauhtémoc</a> was captured. Estimates of the dead in the campaign run from 100,000 to 240,000, and the Indigenous allies went on killing and looting after the surrender.</span></div>
        </div>
