    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Cortés took the city with the help of Indigenous allies, mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlaxcalans">Tlaxcalans</a>, who had been subjugated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a>; they were indispensable to his success.</li><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> epidemic that began in October 1520 killed much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a> leadership, among them the tlatoani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuitlahuac">Cuitlahuac</a>, and weakened a city that the Spaniards then cut off from food and water.</li><li>After the surrender the Indigenous allies slaughtered thousands of civilians; Cortés wrote that he could not prevent more than fifteen thousand being killed and sacrificed in one day.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Cortés ordered thirteen sloops built in Tlaxcala and launched them on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a> in 1521; with them he could open gaps in the causeways and control the water round <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

